[{"id":"29771","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>National Coal Development Corporation (NCDC) was formed in _____ with 11 collieries with the task of exploring new coalfields and expediting development of new coal mines.</span></p>","option_1":"1957","option_2":"1959","option_3":"1955","option_4":"1951","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - 1957.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The National Coal Development Corporation (NCDC) was set up by the Government of India in 1957 with 11 collieries taken over from the East Indian Railway, tasked with exploring new coalfields and speeding up the development of coal mining in the public sector, ahead of the eventual nationalisation of coal mines in India.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29772","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Where is urine stored before it is released from the human body?</span></p>","option_1":"In the kidneys","option_2":"In the ureters","option_3":"In the urinary bladder","option_4":"In the urethra","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - In the urinary bladder.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Urine formed in the kidneys travels through the ureters to the urinary bladder, a muscular sac that stores urine until it is voluntarily released through the urethra during urination (micturition).</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29773","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>In ancient India, the 'Vajjis' had their capital at Vaishali, which was ruled by the_____.</span></p>","option_1":"Mallas","option_2":"Kambojas","option_3":"Kurus","option_4":"Lichchhavis","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"4","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option D - Lichchhavis.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The Vajji Mahajanapada was a confederacy of clans, the most prominent being the Lichchhavis, whose capital was Vaishali. It is regarded as one of the earliest examples of a republican form of government in ancient India.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29774","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>A 'Cut Motion' in Indian parliament is related to_____.</span></p>","option_1":"reducing budget demands","option_2":"removing a judge","option_3":"amending the Constitution","option_4":"dissolving the House","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </