"option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Kavita Kané.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>'The Fisher Queen's Dynasty' is a mythological-fiction work by Kavita Kané, an Indian author known for reimagining stories of women from Indian epics and mythology.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29787","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Which of the following is the objective of India's Industrial Policy 1991?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span> </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>I. To introduce liberalisation.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span> </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>II. To remove restrictions on direct foreign investment.</span></p>","option_1":"Only I","option_2":"Only II","option_3":"Both I and II","option_4":"Neither I nor II","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Both I and II.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The Industrial Policy of 1991 was a landmark reform that introduced liberalisation, privatisation, and globalisation (LPG), abolished industrial licensing for most industries, and significantly eased restrictions on foreign direct investment — so both statements I and II are correct.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29788","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The image represents one of the ways through which a batsman can be given \"out\" in the game of cricket (the illustration shows the bowler's delivery striking and dislodging the stumps directly). What is it called?</span></p>","option_1":"Bowled","option_2":"Hit Wicket","option_3":"Stumped","option_4":"LBW","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Bowled.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>A batsman is given out 'Bowled' when a legally delivered ball from the bowler hits and disturbs the stumps (dislodging a bail), as depicted in the image showing the ball striking the wicket directly.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29789","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The Jaigarh Fort is located in which of the following city?</span></p>","option_1":"Bikaner","option_2":"Ajmer","option_3":"Udaipur","option_4":"Jaipur","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"4","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option D - Jaipur.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Jaigarh Fort is located in Jaipur, Rajasthan, perched on the Cheel ka Teela (Hill of Eagles) above Amber Fort, and was built to protect Amber Fort and its palace complex; it is also known for housing the world's largest cannon on wheels, Jaivana.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29790","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The \"Cancel Coal\" case, which was seen in news in December 2024, is associated with which of the following country?</span></p>","option_1":"South Africa","option_2":"India","option_3":"Vietnam","option_4":"Iran","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - South Africa.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The 'Cancel Coal' case relates to a climate-litigation matter in South Africa concerning the approval and financing of new coal-fired power projects, challenged on environmental and constitutional (right to a healthy environment) grounds.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29791","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Indian wrestlers won _____ medals in Commonwealth Games 2022.</span></p>","option_1":"12","option_2":"10","option_3":"8","option_4":"6","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - 12.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>At the 2022 Commonwealth Games held in Birmingham, Indian wrestlers had a dominant campaign, winning a total of 12 medals in wrestling, including 6 gold medals.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29792","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The '80-pillar hall' was part of the palace of which great emperor?</span></p>","option_1":"Ashoka","option_2":"Samudragupta","option_3":"Chandragupta I","option_4":"Harshavardhana","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Ashoka.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>The remains of an '80-pillared hall' were excavated at Kumrahar near Patna (ancient Pataliputra), believed to be part of the Mauryan royal palace complex associated with Emperor Ashoka's capital.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29793","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Which of the following statement is correct regarding doping?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span> </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>I. EPO is a peptide hormone.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span> </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>II. EPO is released from the kidneys.</span></p>","option_1":"Only I","option_2":"Only II","option_3":"Both I and II","option_4":"Neither I nor II","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Both I and II.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Erythropoietin (EPO) is indeed a peptide hormone, and it is naturally produced and released mainly by the kidneys to stimulate red blood cell production; it is banned in sports as it is misused to artificially boost oxygen-carrying capacity and endurance. Both statements I and II are correct.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29794","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"776","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span>Which country has the largest reserve of iron ore in Asia?</span></p>","option_1":"India","option_2":"China","option_3":"Russia","option_4":"Iran","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","opti